# One secret per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# Consumed by .agent/hooks/_shared/scrub-secrets.py at every point the
# transcript pipeline RETAINS bytes (archive write, demote, promote, and the
# crashed-session orphan sweep).
#
# Copy to .secrets_for_scrubbing_upon_archive.txt (gitignored) and add real
# values. Entries shorter than 16 characters are IGNORED on purpose: a short
# match would redact ordinary text across the whole corpus.
#
# .env values are picked up automatically when the KEY looks like a credential
# (TOKEN/SECRET/KEY/PASSWORD/CREDENTIAL/PAT), so they need not be repeated here.
# This file is for secrets that live nowhere else -- e.g. a token embedded in a
# git remote URL, which is exactly how `git remote -v` banks one in a transcript.
